From 06a6cd7883c99ba5826ed598da1401760776e1cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Hargett <plaztiksyke@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 23:49:26 -0700
Subject: pulley/cranelift: phase-3 fusion (xband + funcref dispatch into one
 op)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 3 of the opcode-fusion track. Extends the phase-2
`FuncrefDispatch` recogniser to ALSO absorb the preceding standalone
`xband_s8` op, emitting one `MInst::BandFuncrefDispatch` that
combines:

  band v, -2          ; mask the funcref init bit
  brif value_masked    ; null check
  xload code @ +8       ; load wasm_call code pointer
  xload vmctx @ +24    ; load callee vmctx

… all into a single Pulley dispatch (`xband_funcref_dispatch_*`).
The dispatch tail at the call_indirect lazy-init site goes from
phase 2's three ops (`xband_s8 ; xfuncref_dispatch_not_x64 ;
call_indirect`) to two (`xband_funcref_dispatch_not_x64 ;
call_indirect`). Saves one more match_loop dispatch per
call_indirect site vs phase 2; four more vs the unfused baseline.

Layered changes:

  pulley/src/lib.rs: 4 new ops (`xband_funcref_dispatch_{x64,
  not_x64, x32, not_x32}`) — same shape as phase 2's
  `xfuncref_dispatch_*` ops but with an additional `dst_masked`
  result. The masked value is written unconditionally (matching
  the original standalone `xband_s8` semantics) so the brif's
  block-call-arg copy to the continuation block still finds it;
  the two field loads are conditional on `src != 0`, same as
  phase 2.

  pulley/src/interp.rs: 4 new handler fns mirroring the op
  semantics.

  cranelift/codegen/src/isa/pulley_shared/inst.isle +
  inst/mod.rs + inst/emit.rs: new `MInst::BandFuncrefDispatch`
  variant carrying 3 dsts (`dst_masked`, `dst_code`, `dst_vmctx`)
  + 1 src + 2 i8 offsets + 2 MachLabels. Operand collector
  reports all three as defs; emit uses the same MachBuffer
  forward/inverted scaffolding as `FuncrefDispatch`.

  cranelift/codegen/meta/src/pulley.rs: skip auto-ISLE-rule
  generation for `XbandFuncrefDispatch*` because the meta
  generator only supports 0/1/2 result vregs (our op has 3).
  The op is emitted only via the hand-written
  `MInst::BandFuncrefDispatch` path, so no auto-rule is needed.

  cranelift/codegen/src/isa/pulley_shared/lower.rs:
  `try_fuse_funcref_dispatch` extended. When the phase-2 pattern
  matches AND cond's def is a band(v, -2), now also sinks the
  band via `sink_pure_inst` and emits `BandFuncrefDispatch` with
  `src = v` (unmasked). The handler does its own masking. Falls
  back to phase 2 (FuncrefDispatch with src = cond, band stays
  standalone) when the band's source can't be cleanly derived.

Tests re-blessed:
  tests/disas/pulley-call-indirect-band-brif-fusion.wat
  tests/disas/pulley-fusion-fires-{32bit,multi-call,return-call-indirect}.wat

The "no-fire" tests (mutable/table-fill/copy/grow, user-mask, sig-
runtime-check) are unchanged — phase 3 is a strict superset of
phase 2's gating, so anywhere phase 2 declines to fire, phase 3
also declines.

Test totals:
    2237 / 2237  cranelift disas
    16 / 16      wasmtime-environ table_mutability
    7 / 7        pulley fusion integration (tests/all/pulley.rs)

Plus a ~21 min differential fuzz run (`cargo fuzz run differential
--no-default-features`, ALLOWED_ENGINES=pulley,wasmtime) found no
crashes or Pulley-vs-native divergences — independent verification
that the three layered fusions don't break correctness.

Soundness same as phase 2: gated on `is_eagerly_initialized_funcref_table`
(via the IR rewrite in `func_environ`) + `mask == -2` (via
width-aware `is_minus_two_for`). The fused op tests the UNMASKED
src for non-zero, valid under the predicate because
`v != 0 <=> (v & -2 != 0)` on every reachable funcref-slot value
in an eagerly-initialised table (the v == 1 tagged-null case is
excluded by the `tables_mutated == false` half of the predicate).
